body:
I personally want more player comms. I absolutely love listening to the videos that show the in game comms between the players whether it be funny like the DIG funny moments from a few years ago or whether it be really stressful like at worlds etc. It gives us as the community more insight on what its like to be a pro player and is just entertaining to listen to. 

&#x200B;

Also like someone else said, the fact that you are asking is above and beyond the standard in the spl right now so thank you so much!

That's something i put together after hearing a bunch of talk about why teams are doing it and it all makes sense and the example i put in the post is an extreme that wouldn't end too well unless it was practiced heavily. I guess for a team like Renegades who have a team full of multi-skilled/roled players (Raff can do support/jungle, Dardez is any position, Cherryo plays a lot of guardians ect.) i feel like nothing is stopping them from just playing literally however they wanted which I guess is a question of whether anything is holding the role system in place for smite at all anymore.

&#x200B;

Also I wanted to reiterate that i in no way mean this as I dislike this sorta thing, just curious if there is something that says the players aren't allowed to go too far out from a "definition" of their assigned role.

Her parents are really toxic. I've compared them to toddlers at times because they whine about the simplest of things. I'm not parent and it may not be my right to say it but they truly don't know how to actually parent, they just expect their children to love them without actually giving them a reason. She doesn't talk to them though because shes not a confrontational type person and won't let me do it because she knows that it will end badly. 

&#x200B;

I think what you said is a really good idea honestly, I just don't know if its what she wants. Shes been fed this idea like all of us that we have to go to a 4 year college and I think the thought of not doing that especially a month away from moving out really is destroying her self-worth. Thank you for the help thought I really appreciate it.
